---
const steps = [
  {
    title: 'Scope call',
    detail:
      'Twenty minutes. I ask how the business actually runs, and tell you honestly whether I can help. If I can’t, I say so and point you elsewhere.',
    output: 'No charge',
  },
  {
    title: 'Written scope, fixed price',
    detail:
      'Within 48 hours you get the deliverables, the timeline, the price and what is explicitly out of scope. Nothing starts until you approve it.',
    output: '48 hours',
  },
  {
    title: 'Weekly working demo',
    detail:
      'Every Friday you get a link to software that actually runs, not a status update. Feedback goes straight into the next week’s build.',
    output: 'Every Friday',
  },
  {
    title: 'Handover, not dependency',
    detail:
      'Repository, database migrations, deployment config, written docs and recorded walkthroughs. Then 30 days of fixes at no extra cost.',
    output: '30 days support',
  },
];
---

<section id="process" class="border-t border-line/70 py-20 sm:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-wide text-accent uppercase">Process</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">You see it working every week.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
        The risk in hiring any developer is not the hourly rate — it's discovering in month
        three that the work isn't what you needed. This process is built so that can't happen
        quietly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="mt-12 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-line bg-line md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {
        steps.map((step, index) => (
          <li class="reveal flex flex-col bg-panel p-6">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-wide text-accent uppercase">
                {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
              </span>
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-wide text-muted/70 uppercase">
                {step.output}
              </span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="mt-5 text-base font-semibold tracking-tight">{step.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{step.detail}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <div
      class="reveal mt-6 grid gap-6 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-panel p-6 sm:p-8 md:grid-cols-3"
    >
      {
        [
          [
            'Fixed price, not estimates',
            'You approve a number before work starts. If I underestimate the effort, that’s my problem, not an extra invoice.',
          ],
          [
            'Two clients at a time',
            'I deliberately cap concurrent builds so the timeline I quote is one I can actually hit.',
          ],
          [
            'You own everything',
            'Code, schema, keys, accounts and documentation are yours at handover. No lock-in, ever.',
          ],
        ].map(([title, body]) => (
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold">{title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
